---
import OptionPage from '../../components/OptionPage.astro';
import prices from '../../data/option-prices.json';
import { link } from '../../data/site.js';

const page = {
  path: '/options/paint-stain-finish/',
  name: 'Paint, Stain & Finish Systems',
  title: 'Shed Exterior Paint, Wood Stain & Finish Systems | Appalachian Sheds',
  description: 'Exterior finish systems for Appalachian Sheds buildings: premium acrylic paint for LP SmartSide and DuraTemp, wood stains for cedar and pine, accent colors and caulking, with planning prices per square foot.',
  h1: 'Paint, Stain & Exterior Finish Systems',
  answer: 'Exterior paint, stain and caulking are not included in the standard building price, but the 30-Year Structural Warranty requires the exterior to be painted within 30 days of completion (vinyl-sided buildings are exempt). You can add paint to your project or have it painted yourself. The surface underneath decides the finish. LP SmartSide and DuraTemp take premium exterior paint, and LP SmartSide is never stained. Cedar and pine can take stain. Factory-colored vinyl normally stays factory-colored. Planning prices run $2.50 to $5.00 per exterior finish square foot for one-color paint and $3.25 to $6.50 for two colors, and finishes are priced by actual surface area, not floor area.',
  familyLabel: 'Finish Topic',
  stepsTitle: 'Protect the Exterior First, Then Choose the Color',
  stepsLead: 'Paint and stain cannot make up for wet material, unprotected cuts, dirt or the wrong sealant. Clean, dry, compatible and properly detailed matters more than buying the most expensive coating.',
  steps: [
    ['Confirm the surface', 'Siding, trim, wood species, door material and factory finish.'],
    ['Clean & dry', 'Remove construction residue; surfaces must be dry before finishing.'],
    ['Protect cut edges', 'Seal or paint exposed cuts per the siding maker’s instructions.'],
    ['Caulk the right joints', 'Compatible sealant only where the detail calls for it.'],
    ['Prime where required', 'Bare wood, repairs and product-specific conditions.'],
    ['Apply & maintain', 'Follow temperature and coat requirements; set a recoat plan.'],
  ],
  families: [
    {
      id: 'by-surface',
      name: 'Finish Compatibility by Siding',
      intro: [
        'LP SmartSide is a paint path, not a stain path: LP’s instructions call for a high-quality exterior paint and say not to use stain. Roseburg DuraTemp takes an acrylic-latex paint system. Georgia-Pacific vinyl keeps its factory color unless a specific product and coating combination is reviewed.',
        'Pine can be painted or stained depending on the application. Cedar can take solid, semi-solid, semi-transparent or transparent stain, tested on the actual wood first.',
      ],
    },
    {
      id: 'systems',
      name: 'Finish Systems & Planning Prices',
      intro: [
        'Price is set by surface area, trim detail, prep and number of colors. Small custom buildings often carry a higher effective rate, because setup, trim and masking remain substantial even when the structure is small.',
      ],
      prices: prices.finish.systems,
      after: 'Planning ranges only. Final pricing depends on actual finish surface, material compatibility, preparation, coating system and the weather window.',
    },
    {
      id: 'stain',
      name: 'Choosing a Wood Stain',
      intro: [
        'More pigment generally means more coverage and protection. The more natural grain you want to see, the more closely the finish needs watching.',
      ],
      bestUses: ['Transparent / clear: maximum grain, least protection, for select accents', 'Semi-transparent: strong grain with color, for cedar and pine', 'Semi-solid: some grain, stronger color and consistency', 'Solid stain: full color that keeps the wood texture'],
    },
    {
      id: 'color',
      name: 'Color Coordination',
      intro: [
        'One body color plus one controlled trim or door accent usually looks more intentional than several competing colors. Color is the last coordination step: siding, then roof, trim, doors and windows, then the accent color.',
      ],
      bestUses: ['Warm neutrals: ivory, cream, taupe, stone, warm gray', 'Earthy greens: sage, olive, deep forest', 'Charcoal accents on doors, trim or hardware', 'Cedar or stained-pine details to warm a painted exterior'],
    },
  ],
  considerationsTitle: 'No Exterior Finish Is Maintenance-Free',
  considerations: [
    ['Paint needs inspection', 'Watch exposed cuts, peeling, impact damage, failed caulk and weathered edges.'],
    ['Clear finishes need the most care', 'Minimal pigment hides less weathering and needs more frequent attention.'],
    ['Dark colors need review', 'Heat limits matter, especially on vinyl.'],
    ['Caulk is not flashing', 'Sealant helps selected joints; it does not replace drainage. Do not caulk every gap.'],
    ['Wood moves', 'Cedar and pine expand, contract and weather differently from engineered siding.'],
    ['Siding & Exterior Materials', 'Choose the siding first; it decides the finish path.', link('/options/siding-exterior-materials/')],
  ],
  faqs: [
    { q: 'Is exterior paint included in the building price?', a: 'No. Exterior paint is priced separately using the finish systems on this page. The building must be painted within 30 days of completion to keep the 30-Year Structural Warranty, either as an Appalachian Sheds option or by the homeowner. Buildings with factory-colored vinyl siding are exempt.' },
    { q: 'How soon must the building be painted?', a: 'Within 30 days of completion. That is a requirement of the Appalachian Sheds 30-Year Structural Warranty. Buildings with factory-colored vinyl siding are exempt.' },
    { q: 'Can LP SmartSide be stained?', a: 'No. LP’s instructions call for a high-quality exterior paint and say not to use stain on LP SmartSide.' },
    { q: 'How much does it cost to paint a shed?', a: 'Planning ranges are $2.50 to $5.00 per exterior finish square foot for one color and $3.25 to $6.50 for two colors, based on actual wall, gable and trim area.' },
    { q: 'Can vinyl siding be painted?', a: 'Factory-colored vinyl normally stays factory-colored. Field coating is considered only after the exact product and coating are reviewed.' },
  ],
  ctaTitle: 'Choose Your Finish and Colors With Edwin',
};
---
<OptionPage page={page} />
